7) HOW TO RUN (quick — copy/paste; paths from ProjectGuardian folder)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Full guided steps (installs, verification, E2E order): **MANUAL_STEPS.md** (authoritative).

OS: Windows 10/11 (agent). Python 3.11+ for brain/dashboard.

Summary only:
  Brain: venv → pip install -r requirements.txt → .env → uvicorn on :8000
  Dashboard: venv → pip → SUPABASE_* env → streamlit run app.py
  Agent: dotnet build → dotnet run (after appsettings + brain URL/key match)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8) KNOWN ISSUES / RISKS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- OCR accuracy: DPI scaling, dark theme, wrong ScreenRegion → empty or wrong text.
- HF: rate limits, cold models, model output shape differences (brain picks max score).
- Security: MVP uses shared API key; service role in dashboard is powerful — lock down for prod.
- Queue: DequeueAll drains entire file on flush; re-queue on failure — OK for MVP.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9) NEXT TODO (ordered, one session each)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Local: dotnet build ProjectGuardian/agent/Guardian.Agent.csproj — fix any WinRT/package errors.
2. Supabase: run schema.sql; confirm brain inserts rows on POST /analyze.
3. End-to-end: run brain → agent with matching BrainApiKey; confirm events in DB.
4. Tune appsettings.json ScreenRegion + whitelist for Discord (or test app).
5. (Optional) Deploy brain to Hugging Face Spaces; set BrainBaseUrl to HTTPS.
6. (Post-MVP) RLS, JWT, pHash, betweenness centrality, hosts/overlay/realtime per plan §12.

